{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>The sons of Menasheh: of Makir.</b> All the tribes were counted here according to the order in which they were counted in the perashah of Bemidbar, except for Menasheh and Efrayim — here Menasheh was placed before Efrayim, because the number of his families exceeded those of Efrayim. In Bemidbar, the families of Efrayim exceeded those of Menasheh, therefore there Efrayim was placed before Menasheh. Moreover, Efrayim was the head of a degel (banner), and in that passage the order of degalim began, so they placed him first. But here, where they were counted for the division of the land, Menasheh was placed before Efrayim because half his tribe took their inheritance first, across the Jordan." "<b>Of Makir.</b> The sons of Makir were divided into eight families: one is named after him, and the other after Gil'ad, and the six after six sons of Gil'ad."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:50.191937429Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}